## Experience and Lessons
|Case|:user_login
```
CLASS UserManager:
    FUNCTION authenticate_user(username, password):
        READ users.txt line by line
        COMPARE credentials with each stored user
        RETURN match status

ROUTE /login:
    IF POST request:
        GET username, password from form
        IF authenticate_user(username, password):
            SET username in session
            REDIRECT to dashboard
        ELSE:
            RENDER login.html with error
    ELSE:
        RENDER login.html
```

```
CLASS UserManager:
    FUNCTION validate_user(username, password):
        READ users.txt
        CHECK IF username AND password MATCH ANY ENTRY
        RETURN True IF MATCH, False IF NOT
END CLASS

ROUTE /login (POST):
    EXTRACT username, password FROM FORM
    IF UserManager.validate_user(username, password):
        SET SESSION['username'] = username
        REDIRECT TO DASHBOARD
    ELSE:
        RENDER login.html WITH ERROR
END ROUTE
```

```
FUNCTION login(username, password)
    users = READ users.txt (format: username|password per line)
    IF username EXISTS AND password MATCHES
        SET current_user = username
        RETURN True
    ELSE
        RETURN False
    ENDIF
END FUNCTION
```

8. |Case|:user_registration
```
FUNCTION register(username, password)
    users = READ users.txt (format: username|password per line)
    IF username EXISTS in users
        RETURN False
    ELSE
        APPEND username|password TO users.txt
        SET current_user = username
        RETURN True
    ENDIF
END FUNCTION
```

