## Experience and Lessons
|Case|:user_registration
Failure Analysis1: No duplicate username validation in registration flow. Always redirects to dashboard even for duplicate registrations. Potential data integrity issues (password overwrite).
Improvement Guidance1: Implement duplicate check in UserManager.register_user(). First scan users.txt for existing username. Only proceed if username is unique. Modify registration route to handle registration failure case and return appropriate error message. Update register.html to display registration errors and maintain form data on failure.
Failure Analysis2: No error message displayed when registering a duplicate username. The test expects `<p style="color: red;">` but the error might not render correctly.
Improvement Guidance2: Ensure error rendering in register.html. Verify the error message is correctly passed to the template. Check if the template properly displays errors (e.g., missing `{{ error }}`). Improve error handling in UserManager.create_user() by logging errors when file operations fail and returning specific error messages.

2. |Case|:join_study_groups
Failure Analysis1: New group not appearing in the list after creation. GroupManager.join_group() may fail silently (exception caught but not logged). The file (groups.txt) might not be updated correctly.
Improvement Guidance1: Debug file operations in GroupManager.join_group(). Log whether the file is being written. Verify file permissions. Ensure atomic updates using file locking to prevent race conditions. Add error logging for file I/O failures. Improve group listing by verifying groups.html correctly displays all groups from groups.txt.
Failure Analysis2: Joined groups not displayed due to missing current_user in template context and groups data not refreshed after modification.
Improvement Guidance2: Always pass current_user to all templates that need it. Implement proper session management instead of class variable. Either refresh groups data after modification or use proper database transactions.

